<title>UK: TABLE-CIA Group hit by exceptionals in 96.</title>
<headline>TABLE-CIA Group hit by exceptionals in 96.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, pre-excep) 7.88		   vs 7.65</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.77		   vs 1.62</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 2.35		   vs 2.16</p>
<p> Pretax		     4.92		   vs 6.68</p>
<p> Turnover		   773.77		 vs 606.40</p>
<p>Full company name - CIA Group Plc.</p>
<p>NOTE - CIA, Europe's second largest independent media buyer, said its 1996 results included 2.58 million stg in exceptional costs. These related to the settlement of a dispute over the purchase of UK television airtime and the loss on the disposal of a subsidiary.</p>
<p>The company said pre-tax, pre-exceptional profits showed a 12 percent rise on 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
